{% doc %}
won-product-schema — emit a supplementary Product JSON-LD node carrying
`additionalProperty` (spec / nutrition facts) so search and AI answer engines can
read the product's attributes as structured data.

Rendered by the ROW block (won-param-table / won-nutrition-table), NOT the
section: a section can't read its child theme-blocks' settings through
`{% content_for 'blocks' %}`, so each table self-emits (see repo memory /
[[won-schema-engine]]). The node is keyed by the canonical product URL as `@id`
+ `url`, so search/AI engines merge it onto the product — including Shopify's own
Product node from the `structured_data` filter — instead of creating a duplicate.
Several blocks on one PDP share the `@id` and merge into one property list.

Honesty/safety guards: emits nothing off a product page, when disabled, or when
there is no valid name/value pair. `| json` encodes every value; `</` is
neutralised so FAQ/spec text can never break out of the script.

@param {boolean} enabled - the block's emit_schema toggle
@param {string} mode - 'lines' | 'kv' | 'none'
@param {string} separator - cell separator for lines mode (':' specs, '|' nutrition)
@param line_items - array/string of "name<sep>value" rows (lines mode)
@param kv_value - parsed JSON object of name/value pairs (kv mode)
@example
{% render 'won-product-schema', enabled: block.settings.emit_schema, mode: mode, separator: ':', line_items: line_items, kv_value: kv_value %}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  assign props = ''
  if enabled and product != blank
    if mode == 'kv'
      for property in kv_value
        assign pk = property.first | strip_html | strip
        assign pv = property.last | strip_html | strip
        if pk != blank and pv != blank
          capture frag
            echo '{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":'
            echo pk | json
            echo ',"value":'
            echo pv | json
            echo '}'
          endcapture
          if props != blank
            assign props = props | append: ','
          endif
          assign props = props | append: frag
        endif
      endfor
    elsif mode == 'lines'
      for line in line_items
        assign row = line | strip
        assign cells = row | split: separator
        assign pk = cells[0] | strip_html | strip
        assign pv = cells[1] | strip_html | strip
        if pk != blank and pv != blank
          capture frag
            echo '{"@type":"PropertyValue","name":'
            echo pk | json
            echo ',"value":'
            echo pv | json
            echo '}'
          endcapture
          if props != blank
            assign props = props | append: ','
          endif
          assign props = props | append: frag
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endif
  assign canonical = product.url | prepend: shop.url
-%}
{%- if props != blank -%}
  {%- capture won_prod_json -%}{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Product","@id":{{ canonical | json }},"url":{{ canonical | json }},"name":{{ product.title | json }},"additionalProperty":[{{ props }}]}{%- endcapture -%}
  <script type="application/ld+json">{{ won_prod_json | replace: '</', '<\/' }}</script>
{%- endif -%}
